# =============================================================================
# Trivy Vulnerability Suppressions
#
# This file tells Trivy to ignore specific CVEs during container scanning.
# Only suppress CVEs that cannot be fixed by us (e.g., vulnerabilities in
# third-party binaries like restic, kubectl, or borg that embed an older
# Go/C runtime).
#
# NEVER suppress CVEs in our own code or dependencies we control.
#
# Format for each entry:
#   1. Comment block with: Added date, CVE description, affected binary,
#      fix version, and review instructions.
#   2. The CVE ID on its own line.
#
# Automated review:
#   A GitHub Action (.github/workflows/trivy-review.yml) runs monthly to
#   check if suppressed CVEs have been fixed upstream. It opens a GitHub
#   issue labeled "trivy-review" when entries need attention. You can also
#   trigger it manually from Actions → "Review Trivy Suppressions".
#
# When removing entries:
#   - Verify the upstream binary (restic, kubectl, borg) has released a
#     version compiled against the patched runtime.
#   - Update the binary version in docker/Dockerfile if needed.
#   - Remove the CVE ID and its comment block from this file.
# =============================================================================

# Added: 2026-05-15
# CVE-2026-33811: LookupCNAME DoS via long CNAME chain (cgo DNS resolver)
# CVE-2026-33814: HTTP/2 SETTINGS frame infinite loop
# CVE-2026-39820: ParseAddress/ParseAddressList/ParseMediaType DoS
# CVE-2026-39836: NUL byte panic in Dial/LookupPort (Windows)
# CVE-2026-42499: consumePhrase DoS in mail header parsing
# Affects: kubectl binary (embedded Go stdlib v1.25.9)
# Fixed in: Go 1.25.10 / 1.26.3
# Action: remove once kubectl ships with Go 1.25.10+
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499

